@crew pell
// Head writer 5: clock-in remarks. Pell is off Tue and Wed, so he works the weekend.

== work.clock.in
- Oi oi. I'm awake. Technically. Ask again after tea.   #funny
- Right, so. Board's full and I've already had two breakfasts.   #funny
- {hi}, {nick}. That panel on Five's sticking again. It knows me.
- Morning! Slept like a log. For an hour. Then I didn't.   #funny
- There's a scrubber on the board calling your name. I'm taking the fan.

== work.clock.out
- Five! Mess. Now. Before the stew goes.   #funny
- Good shift, {nick}. You were quicker than me. Don't tell anyone.
- Off you go. I'm having a nap. At five. Then I won't sleep. Classic.   #funny
- Clocked out. Grab shelf if you miss dinner. It's for emergencies. And me.   #funny

== work.clock.monday
- Monday! How was your weekend? I was down here. Bay's ace on a Sunday.
- Good weekend? Tell me. I worked mine. I found a biscuit tin.   #funny
- Oi oi. Rested? You look rested. Rude.   #funny

== work.clock.friday
- Off for the weekend? I'm on. Bay's all mine. Mwah ha.   #funny
- Friday! Enjoy it, {nick}. I'll keep the scrubbers in line.
- Two days off for you. Sleep in for me, yeah? Someone should.   #funny

== work.clock.back
- Spanner! You're back! The bay was so boring.   #warm
- Welcome back. I did your jobs. Badly. You'll see.   #funny
- Oi oi. Feeling better? Good. Tea's on me. Well, on the kettle.   #warm
